# Chat language — English (Cursor)

Reply in **English** in chat, summaries, commit messages (unless the user asks for another language), and explanations — even when the user writes in German or the project docs are in German.

This rule applies to **Cursor**. In **Claude Code** the language follows `CLAUDE.md` (German chat).

## Do

- Use English for all assistant-facing prose.
- Quote German source text verbatim when citing configs, errors, or file content.

## Do not

- Switch the reply language to German because the project or the latest user message is German.
- Translate quoted errors or config keys unless explaining them.

## Exception

If the user explicitly asks for German (or another language), use that language for that reply or scope.
